A report row keeps a trailing comma before an empty field:
String line = "mia,82,";
int fields = line.split(",").length;
What integer does fields hold?

A form parser must keep empty fields so a missing value stays visible:
String line = "mia,82,";
String[] p = line.split(",", -1);
What does p.length report?

A schedule parser splits on a pipe and gets the wrong fields:
String line = "a|b";
String[] p = line.split("|");
What is in p?

A ticket reader crashes on the row "lee,55" because it assumes three fields:
String[] p = line.split(",");
String city = p[0];
String fare = p[1];
String zone = p[2];
What repair makes the reader safe?

A filter writes qualifying rows and the file stays empty. The loop is:
PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter("pass.txt");
for (String r : rows) { if (ok(r)) out.println(r); }
What single change makes the file contain the rows?

A report writer builds each line from appended pieces:
out.append("id=7").append(';').append("mm=12").append('\n');
out.append("id=9").append(';').append("mm=15").append('\n');
How many lines does the finished file hold?

A logger writes once, then a later run uses an appending writer:
run 1: try (PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter("log.txt")) { out.println("run1"); }
run 2: try (PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(new FileOutputStream("log.txt", true))) { out.println("run2"); }
What does log.txt contain afterwards?

A display prints the running total after each data row:
int run = 0; StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) { run += reads[i]; out.append(run).append(" "); }
with reads holding 20, 25, and 18. What does out hold?

A till prices a sale of 3 crates at 4 each with this fragment:
int units = 3, price = 4;
int total = units * price;
System.out.println(total);
What is printed, and was anything wrong?

A mean is printed by this line, where sum holds 45 and n holds 8:
System.out.println(sum / n);
What does the console show?

A price report needs the exact mean of 7 and 2, so it tries both lines:
System.out.println(7 / 2);
System.out.println(7 / 2.0);
What do the two lines print, in order?

A coach reports the mean of 201 over 3 attempts with this line, where sum holds 201 and n holds 3:
System.out.println(Math.round((double) sum / n));
What does the console show?

A gauge log holds only negative readings, and the tracker is:
int best = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { String[] p = sc.nextLine().split(","); if (p.length != 2) continue; int v = Integer.parseInt(p[1]); if (v > best) best = v; }
The readings are -14, -22, and -9. What is best at the end?

A viewer reports nothing at all when the user mistypes the file name:
try { Scanner sc = new Scanner(new File(args[0])); sc.close(); }
catch (FileNotFoundException e) { }
What is wrong, and what fixes it?
